(7109809, 1083874, 112828, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by P-A-U-L:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by skewsme:</b></div><hr/><i> congrats...very cute - but hard to believe that''s a 1/40s exposure unless you used a tripod and they''re stuffed ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well spotted! I did indeed use a tripod that morning as I was using my new Canon 10-22 lens and thought as it did not have Image Stabilisation it would need a helping hand to keep things steady. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>@10mm you should be able to hand-hold a 1/20 with ease.</td>', 'Originally posted by P-A-U-L: Originally posted by skewsme: congrats...very cute - but hard to believe that''s a 1/40s exposure unless you used a tripod and they''re stuffed ;-)   Well spotted! I did indeed use a tripod that morning as I was using my new Canon 10-22 lens and thought as it did not have Image Stabilisation it would need a helping hand to keep things steady.   @10mm you should be able to hand-hold a 1/20 with ease.', '2013-10-02 12:29:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7109813, 1083874, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Cory:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by P-A-U-L:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by skewsme:</b></div><hr/><i> congrats...very cute - but hard to believe that''s a 1/40s exposure unless you used a tripod and they''re stuffed ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well spotted! I did indeed use a tripod that morning as I was using my new Canon 10-22 lens and thought as it did not have Image Stabilisation it would need a helping hand to keep things steady. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>@10mm you should be able to hand-hold a 1/20 with ease. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Cory, apart from this particular shoot, I have been using my 10-22 hand held at all other times and the results have been grand. I just took the tripod that day as it was quite early morning so the light was a bit low and also the tripod was a good weapon should the cows decide to attack me:)</td>', 'Originally posted by Cory: Originally posted by P-A-U-L: Originally posted by skewsme: congrats...very cute - but hard to believe that''s a 1/40s exposure unless you used a tripod and they''re stuffed ;-)   Well spotted! I did indeed use a tripod that morning as I was using my new Canon 10-22 lens and thought as it did not have Image Stabilisation it would need a helping hand to keep things steady.   @10mm you should be able to hand-hold a 1/20 with ease.   Thanks Cory, apart from this particular shoot, I have been using my 10-22 hand held at all other times and the results have been grand. I just took the tripod that day as it was quite early morning so the light was a bit low and also the tripod was a good weapon should the cows decide to attack me:)', '2013-10-02 12:35:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7109819, 1083478, 12611, '<td valign="top">Beautiful photo Peter, well seen and well processed.(and to think that I lived on the more rural- farm side of CT!)</td>', 'Beautiful photo Peter, well seen and well processed.(and to think that I lived on the more rural- farm side of CT!)', '2013-10-02 12:44:57.000000', NULL, 0),
