(7109878, 1083874, 50641, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Cory:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by P-A-U-L:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by skewsme:</b></div><hr/><i> congrats...very cute - but hard to believe that''s a 1/40s exposure unless you used a tripod and they''re stuffed ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Well spotted! I did indeed use a tripod that morning as I was using my new Canon 10-22 lens and thought as it did not have Image Stabilisation it would need a helping hand to keep things steady. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>@10mm you should be able to hand-hold a 1/20 with ease. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>you can hold it all you want but it doesn''t stop cows from moving ;-)<br/>anyway thanks Paul for the response.</td>', 'Originally posted by Cory: Originally posted by P-A-U-L: Originally posted by skewsme: congrats...very cute - but hard to believe that''s a 1/40s exposure unless you used a tripod and they''re stuffed ;-)  Well spotted! I did indeed use a tripod that morning as I was using my new Canon 10-22 lens and thought as it did not have Image Stabilisation it would need a helping hand to keep things steady.  @10mm you should be able to hand-hold a 1/20 with ease.  you can hold it all you want but it doesn''t stop cows from moving ;-)anyway thanks Paul for the response.', '2013-10-02 13:35:08.000000', NULL, 0),
